            <ArticleTitle>Temporary sedation with midazolam for control of severe incident pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>439-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Incident pain frequently complicates cancer-related pain. Its treatment is sometimes very difficult due to poor responsiveness to opioids. Two cases are presented in which a temporary or intermittent sedation with midazolam was successfully used to control excruciating incident pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
